    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3291666a-ab1b-5845-b6d8-e87ba1f60430",
      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-9{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -7{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2} &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that the system is already organized so that the variables are in the order ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient.\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-9 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 8 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
